{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794045131,"nonce":"PSmLFM2+Uom/Eq6laKWkMHZtbtA=","message":"Cause found with on-device logging via a LAN proxy. On iOS the tap moved focus from the hidden editor to the tabindex canvas (compat mousedown default), the host reported that blur to the demo, which dropped its text input; the editor was refocused but the demo no longer had focus, so the keyboard stayed up and typing went nowhere. The first fix also dropped the keyboard on a fixed 400 ms timer, earlier than the worker's late state report. Fixes: canvas mousedown is default-prevented, a blur to the canvas is not reported, the keyboard drops only on a state report that answers a sync sent after the tap, and the editor is re-focused after the mode is on. Confirmed working on the owner's iPhone via the proxy (input and textarea); Android Chrome not yet checked.","files":null}]}